{{/*
  error — the full-page deck-error shell.

  internal/server serves this page, as the current state of the presentation,
  whenever the watched deck fails validation: exactly one author-facing error,
  the string produced by internal/validate.Format ("file:line › path: what —
  fix"). The terminal prints the identical string, so the author sees one
  message in both places (requirements.requirement.error-reporting,
  requirements.requirement.live-reload-error-page).

  It is a standalone page: OFFLINE, referencing only the embedded reveal.js
  runtime and the project's own theme stylesheet (served under /assets/,
  resolved through the theme registry — theme-selection), never a CDN or any
  network location (global.constraint.go-static-embedded-binary). The page
  carries no brand asset of its own: every colour, font and spacing value it
  uses is a token the project's theme stylesheet defines
  (global.constraint.theme-tokens-only).

  Embedding / access:
    The pages sub-tree is embedded by internal/assets and exposed as
    assets.Pages() (an fs.FS rooted at pages/), so this file's path is
    "error.html.tmpl". internal/server does, in effect:

      template.Must(template.New("error").
          ParseFS(assets.Pages(), "error.html.tmpl"))

    parsing the page in its own template namespace (each page is standalone).

  Execution context (a struct or map[string]any supplying these keys):
    .Title    string   the document <title>. Empty falls back to "eypres".
    .Message  string   the single author-facing error, exactly as
                       validate.Format(verr) rendered it. Shown verbatim and
                       html/template-escaped. Empty falls back to a generic
                       sentence; internal/server always sets it.

  Hook slots:
    "live-reload" is a named block, exactly like the deck page's, so
    internal/server overrides it with {{ define "live-reload" }} before
    parsing and injects its SSE client script there. Because the error page
    carries the same block as deck.html.tmpl, a fixing edit reloads the page
    back to the deck without a manual refresh (live-reload).
*/}}

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ with .Title }}{{ . }}{{ else }}eypres{{ end }}</title>

  {{/* The project's theme stylesheet: its @font-face rules (if any) and the
       token block every rule below consumes. Served from the project's
       theme directory, resolved by internal/server's media handler. */}}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css">
  <style>
    /* Page chrome only, consuming the tokens the theme stylesheet declares;
       no colour, font or spacing value is restated here
       (global.constraint.theme-tokens-only). */
    html, body { margin: 0; }
    body {
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      padding: var(--ey-space-5);
      background: var(--ey-bg-dark);
      color: var(--ey-fg-on-dark);
      font-family: var(--ey-font-body);
      line-height: var(--ey-line-height);
    }
    .ey-error { width: var(--ey-content-width); max-width: 60rem; }
    .ey-error__heading {
      font-family: var(--ey-font-display);
      font-size: var(--ey-font-size-title);
      margin: var(--ey-space-4) 0 var(--ey-space-3);
    }
    .ey-error__message {
      margin: 0 0 var(--ey-space-4);
      padding: var(--ey-space-3);
      border: var(--ey-border-width) solid var(--ey-highlight);
      border-radius: var(--ey-radius);
      background: var(--ey-ink-soft);
      color: var(--ey-highlight);
      font-family: var(--ey-font-mono);
      font-size: var(--ey-font-size-body);
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    .ey-error__hint {
      color: var(--ey-grey-light);
      font-size: var(--ey-font-size-small);
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="ey-error">
    <h1 class="ey-error__heading">Deck error</h1>
    <pre class="ey-error__message">{{ with .Message }}{{ . }}{{ else }}The deck could not be loaded.{{ end }}</pre>
    <p class="ey-error__hint">Fix the file shown above and save; this page reloads automatically.</p>
  </main>

  {{/* Phase-7 live-reload client script is injected here by internal/server. */}}
  {{ block "live-reload" . }}{{ end }}
</body>
</html>
